{"step_index":2475,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-27T10:52:58Z","input_tokens":2640,"cache_read_tokens":201268,"output_tokens":1856,"thinking":"Need to modify the dashboard JavaScript file to incorporate a mechanism for managing active solution approaches. This involves initializing a data structure within the constructor to store the chosen approach for each problem. Also, a new function is needed to retrieve problem solution data, ensuring it leverages a global function if available in the execution environment.\n\n\nThe `getProblemSolutions` function needs implementation, it first attempts to retrieve solution data via a global function. If the global function fails, a fallback is used that creates a default optimized solution. This fallback ensures the system functions even when the external data source is unavailable.\n\nNext, within the `renderProblemWorkspace` function, the code retrieves the solution data using the new function, and then determines the active approach ID based on the stored user preference or falling back to the second or first available solution. This ensures user selected approaches are preserved. Then it renders UI elements based on the unlocked state.\n\n\nThe UI elements for displaying and switching between solution approaches need to be constructed. Approach tabs will include badges for baseline and optimal solutions. A metadata bar will show time and space complexity with a verification badge. The code preview will feature copy and visualizer buttons alongside the code block. Finally, educational sections explaining the algorithm, its rationale, and common pitfalls are needed.\n\nEvent binding updates in the JavaScript file are required to handle switching solution approaches via the new approach tabs.\n\n\nEvent handling for approach switching, solution hiding, and code copying needs implementation.  Specifically, the code needs to respond to clicks on approach selection tabs to update the UI.  Also, buttons for hiding/revealing solutions and copying code to the editor require corresponding event listeners to manage state changes and data transfers.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"Select-String -Path \"app_build\\dsa_dashboard.js\" -Pattern \"showProblemModal\" | Select-Object -First 5","Cwd":"C:\\Users\\CVT\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\code-flow-visualizer","IsDaemon":false,"WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Searching showProblemModal","toolSummary":"Find line for showProblemModal"}}]}
